//Phase 13 Step 1: a void return slot inside the func type ARGUMENTS is
//a SYNTAX error — the void slot exists only in the func type grammar
//(bare base name followed by KT_Void), not in TypeList, which every
//`func<...>` value spelling consumes. (0.9.0: `new` is an ordinary
//identifier, so this fixture also pins the old spelling as a plain
//syntax error.)
int main() {
    func<int, int> f = new func<void, int>();
    return 0;
}
